// REDESIGN PROTOTYPE - "IDE" - Concept 43.
// The portfolio opened inside a real code editor (VS Code-like). Original concept (NOT a reskin):
// its own layout + interaction + palette + fonts + mechanic. This is unmistakably a CODE EDITOR -
// activity bar + file-explorer tree + tab strip + line-number gutter + git-diff gutter + syntax-
// highlighted panels + integrated terminal + minimap + status bar + Cmd+K command palette.
//  - Career rendered as source files: hero.md (name/role/lede), work.json (6 engagements),
//    skills.ts (4 disciplines as a typed const), metrics.sql (a SELECT whose result-set carries the
//    3 hard numbers), about.md (facts + recognition + brands + shipped), contact.sh (real mailto +
//    linkedin links). Clicking a tree file or a tab switches the active editor panel (client JS).
//  - Integrated terminal TYPES "npm run career" then prints build output ending in the 3 metrics +
//    a green "shipped" line. A caret blinks. Reduced-motion shows the final terminal instantly.
//  - GitHub-dark palette (bg #0d1117, activity #010409, panels #161b22, ink #e6edf3, accent #58a6ff)
//    with real syntax colors. JetBrains Mono for the editor, Inter for the chrome.
// GOTCHA NOTES: every file panel lives in the DOM. With JS OFF (no `.js` class on <html>) the CSS
//   fallback shows ALL panels stacked so all content (work + metrics + contact) stays visible; the
//   editor body is not clipped. With JS ON only the active panel shows. prefers-reduced-motion kills
//   the caret blink + typing + reveals and shows the terminal fully built. No text-shadow/filter on
//   any background-clip:text element. Real <a> for email (mailto) and LinkedIn.

// ---- syntax token helpers (compose colored spans for set:html) ----
const k  = (s) => `<span class="tk-k">${s}</span>`;    // keyword
const st = (s) => `<span class="tk-s">${s}</span>`;    // string
const fn = (s) => `<span class="tk-f">${s}</span>`;    // function
const nu = (s) => `<span class="tk-n">${s}</span>`;    // number
const cm = (s) => `<span class="tk-c">${s}</span>`;    // comment
const vr = (s) => `<span class="tk-v">${s}</span>`;    // variable
const pr = (s) => `<span class="tk-prop">${s}</span>`; // json/prop key
const pn = (s) => `<span class="tk-p">${s}</span>`;    // punctuation
// ---- markdown token helpers ----
